.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MANET-MESH-CENSUS.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm manet-mesh-census.py
.Nd summarize traffic observed on the BATMAN mesh port
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -minutes Ar duration
.Op Fl -max-rows Ar count
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
passively observes Ethernet frames on Linux
.Li bat0
and prints a JSON summary at the end of the capture.
It requires root or
.Dv CAP_NET_RAW .
It sends no probes, changes no firewall rules and saves no packet payloads.
Pressing Ctrl-C during capture prints a partial summary.
.Pp
Rows group packets and Ethernet bytes by direction, inferred source bridge
port, source MAC, protocol, transport ports, destination and visible VLANs.
Incoming packets are observed before bridge filtering.
Outgoing packets have passed bridge filtering but do not prove remote delivery.
Source attribution is inferred from periodic local snapshots.
Kernel drops, snapshot failures and row overflow are reported explicitly.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -minutes Ar duration
Capture duration in minutes; default 5.
Must be finite, greater than zero and no greater than 1440.
.It Fl -max-rows Ar count
Maximum distinct detail rows; default 20000, range 1 through 100000.
Excess traffic still contributes to totals and overflow counts.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after printing a report, including a partial capture stopped by Ctrl-C.
Exits 1 for an operating error and 2 for invalid arguments.
A zero status does not imply a lossless capture; check the reported counters.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo manet-mesh-census.py --minutes 5 > /tmp/mesh-census.json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr verify-bridge.sh 8
